              "title": "Untitled Multiple Choice"
            },
            "subContentId": "e2a33c4b-34d2-4a4d-a896-0d59a7c52907"
          },
          {
            "params": {
              "media": {
                "disableImageZooming": false
              },
              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Magnesium hydroxide is an antacid that is osmotically active and not absorbed. As such it causes diarrhoea in many people.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Aluminium hydroxide or citrate is an antacid that causes constipation and also binds to many drugs and nutrients so care should be taken not to take them with meals or medications.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Calcium carbonate has the strongest antacid effects but also has the strongest rebound hyperacidity</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>This one should not have been selected because it is incorrect. Sodium bicarbonate is absorbed and has a lot of sodium in it, so it is not the preferred antacid.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>You are correct, the statement is incorrect. Sodium bicarbonate is absorbed and has a lot of sodium in it, so it is not the preferred antacid.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Sodium bicarbonate is the preferred antacid because it is not absorbed</div>\n"
                }
              ],
